  keywords = {transient ischemic attack, stroke risk, ABCD2, urgent assessment, secondary prevention},
  note    = {Retrospective, n=261 TIA patients, urgent Stroke-Unit assessment + immediate prevention; follow-up to 2 y. Stroke incidence 1.5% at 1 month, 3.4% at 1 year, 4.2% at end of follow-up; median 90 d to recurrence; ABCD2 score poorly predictive. Population weight 0.75 (general TIA/stroke). Supports that NEW focal symptoms must be treated as possible TIA/stroke with urgent assessment — urgent referral is the safety-netting message, not benign attribution to ME/CFS.},
