  note = {VIEWPOINT (no primary data). Proposes a translational framework linking Long Covid and AD(H)D through four converging neuroimmune mechanisms: (1) frontal--striatal--hippocampal dysfunction (catecholaminergic/glutamatergic/GABAergic, neuron senescence); (2) neuroimmune dysregulation of catecholamine systems (T-cell/microglia/macrophage, cytokine imbalance, ANS neuroimmune communication); (3) dysregulated tryptophan--kynurenine metabolism (neurotoxic/pro-inflammatory metabolites); (4) mitochondrial bioenergetic defects (oxidative stress, ROS). Reports off-label ADHD pharmacotherapy in LC (methylphenidate, guanfacine, low-dose lithium, dexamfetamine) with partial response; proposes an acquired 'neuroimmune-mediated dopaminergic/noradrenergic dysfunction' hypothesis and a precision-immunopsychiatry immune-subtyping framework. Population weight 0.85 (Long Covid content; framework relevant to ME/CFS cross-disease). Viewpoint = low raw certainty for the framework itself.},
